The key UX shift

I would define the next UI/UX phase around this principle:

> The system has become intelligent enough that the interface should stop behaving like a collection of tools.



The student should experience it as one preparation system.

Instead of:

“Choose what feature you want to use.”

the product should increasingly say:

“This is where you are. This is what you need. Here's why. Let's do it.”

That is the biggest UX opportunity created by the six-sprint consolidation.
